### 5. Deadline Schema
```typescript
interface Deadline {
  _id: ObjectId;
  title: string;
  start: Date;
  end: Date;
  type: 'application' | 'interview' | 'start_date' | 'school_deadline' | 'other';
  description?: string;
  location?: string;
  color?: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}

// Zod validation schema
const deadlineSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1),
  start: z.string().datetime(),
  end: z.string().datetime(),
  type: z.enum(['application', 'interview', 'start_date', 'school_deadline', 'other']),
  description: z.string().optional(),
  location: z.string().optional(),
  color: z.string().optional(),
});
```

## Refactoring Plan

### Phase 1: Create Shared Types
1. Create new type definition files:
   ```
   src/types/
   ├── location.ts
   ├── profile.ts
   ├── application.ts
   ├── opportunity.ts
   ├── hour-log.ts
   └── deadline.ts
   ```

2. Define shared interfaces:
   ```typescript
   // location.ts
   interface Location {
     address: string;
     city: string;
     state: string;
     zipCode: string;
     coordinates: {
       lat: number;
       lng: number;
     };
   }

   // profile.ts
   interface BaseProfile {
     userId: string;
     skills: string[];
     interests: string[];
     bio?: string;
     createdAt: Date;
     updatedAt: Date;
   }

   interface StudentProfile extends BaseProfile {
     // Student-specific fields
   }

   interface FacilityProfile extends BaseProfile {
     // Facility-specific fields
   }
   ```

### Phase 2: Model Refactoring
1. Update Mongoose models to use shared types
2. Implement proper inheritance
3. Add validation and middleware
4. Update indexes

### Phase 3: Component Updates
1. Update all components to use new type definitions
2. Remove duplicate interface definitions
3. Ensure type safety

### Phase 4: Database Migration
1. Create migration scripts
2. Update existing data
3. Ensure backward compatibility

